  "forced": {
    "why": "REVISION 9 - mobile optimisation and complete handoff. A new audit (tools/audit-mobile.js) measures tap targets and the gaps between them, type size, form-control size, viewport meta, unwrappable text, sticky chrome, and over-delivered images. KEY FINDING: 39 of 42 images already had smaller renditions on disk from the crawl, and exactly 1 of 259 img tags used them - phones were pulling full desktop photographs. Fixed with srcset on 199 tags, where the sizes attribute is the MEASURED rendered width of each image at 390/768/1024/1440 across all 44 routes (audit/image-widths.json), not a guess; an image that was never measured gets no srcset, because a wrong sizes makes the browser pick a worse file than none. Three groups had no small rendition and were downscaled from their own masters with no generative step: the header logo (on all 44 pages, shipping 988px for a 190px box and 644px for a 139px box), the 12 generated slots (single rendition, 1200px for a 335px tile), and the Hyder cut-out (153KB PNG drawn at 179px). MEASURED RESULT across all 44 routes at 390px: image payload 16.80 MB -> 5.78 MB, a 65.6% reduction, average page 391 KB -> 134 KB. The header logo also declared height=200 for a 988x176 file; dimensions are now read from the file. Adjacent pills/go-links measured 7-8px apart in three containers and are now 12px. Mobile is CLEAN: 0 findings at 360/390/414/768 across 16 pages. THREE FALSE POSITIVES WERE REMOVED RATHER THAN ACTED ON, each of which would have caused damage: 96 'small tap targets' were field labels (padding them to 44px would have wrecked every form), 132 of 139 'crowded' pairs were a label and its own input, and 81 'small text' findings were pills and eyebrows which are labels not reading matter. A fourth looked serious - 24 inputs at 13.3px, which makes iOS zoom on focus - but they are the appointment form's HONEYPOT, parked by chrome.css at left:-9999px inside a 1px overflow:hidden box; the audit counted an off-screen element as visible, and 'fixing' it would have meant styling a spam trap into visibility. Also corrected: /contact/ and /appointments/ do not exist as routes, so every earlier sweep had been auditing a 404 page for them; the route list is now generated from dist. HANDOFF: sr-package does not ship tools/, which is the whole build system, so tools/package-handoff.mjs writes a complete archive - everything here plus tools/ plus a root HANDOFF.md covering deploy and server config, rebuild steps, what each audit measures, the stylesheet-order specificity trap, what was done deliberately, and an explicit Known gaps table led by the deliberately unwired appointment form - plus HANDOFF-INVENTORY.json with a SHA-256 per shipped file. Final: mobile audit 0 findings, visual 0 and alignment 0 across 16 pages x 6 viewports (96 runs), spacing 3 (text-beside-text, explained in revision 8), 0 broken images, 0 horizontal overflow, text 100.000% verbatim, refs 6273 with 0 blockers/majors/orphans, parity 0 blockers / 0 majors / 2 pre-existing minors, fabrication SOURCED, decontamination CLEAN. 26/28 PASS; C22 is pixel-parity with the SOURCE which a deliberate redesign must fail, C28 is compose-from-presets while this design layer is authored."
  },
